{"created": "2026-09-12T10:15:22.450673+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-12T10:15:22.902210+00:00", "id": 22722075, "conceptrecid": "22722074", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722075", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722074", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722075", "metadata": {"title": "Failure of finite isolated generation for an irreducible centralizer over a polycyclic group", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722075", "publication_date": "2026-09-12", "description": "<p>Let \\(G=\\mathbb Z^2\\rtimes_M\\mathbb Z\\), where \\(M=\\left(\\begin{smallmatrix}2&amp;1\\\\1&amp;1\\end{smallmatrix}\\right)\\), and let \\(t\\) generate the cyclic factor. The equation \\([x,t]=1\\) defines an infinite irreducible algebraic set over the two-generated torsion-free polycyclic group \\(G\\leq\\mathrm{SL}_3(\\mathbb Z)\\). We prove that its radical in \\(G*\\langle x\\rangle\\) is not the normal isolated closure of any finite subset. Thus no finite equivalent system has radical equal to its normal isolated closure, giving a negative answer to Problem 14.22 of the Kourovka Notebook. The proof identifies the radical as the kernel of a scalar Laurent collection homomorphism. Alternating bilinear extensions then provide torsion-free separating groups for arbitrary finite families of radical equations.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jayadevan, Achyuth", "affiliation": "Manipal Institute of Technology, MAHE", "orcid": "0009-0008-8745-4078"}], "keywords": ["Kourovka Problem 14.22", "Algebraic geometry over groups", "Polycyclic groups", "Radicals", "Nullstellensatz", "Lean 4"], "version": "1.0.0", "references": ["G. Baumslag, A. Myasnikov and V. Remeslennikov, Algebraic geometry over groups I: Algebraic sets and ideal theory, Journal of Algebra 219 (1999), 16\u201379. https://doi.org/10.1006/jabr.1999.7881", "O. Kharlampovich and A. Myasnikov, Irreducible affine varieties over a free group. II. Systems in triangular quasi-quadratic form and description of residually free groups, Journal of Algebra 200 (1998), 517\u2013570. https://doi.org/10.1006/jabr.1997.7184", "E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), The Kourovka Notebook: Unsolved Problems in Group Theory, 21st ed., 2026, updated 1 September 2026, Problem 14.22. https://kourovkanotebookorg.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/21tkt.pdf", "A. Myasnikov and V. Remeslennikov, Algebraic geometry over groups II. Logical foundations, Journal of Algebra 234 (2000), 225\u2013276. https://doi.org/10.1006/jabr.2000.8414", "N. S. Romanovskiy, Hilbert's Nullstellensatz in algebraic geometry over rigid soluble groups, Izvestiya: Mathematics 79 (2015), 1051\u20131063. https://doi.org/10.1070/IM2015v079n05ABEH002771"], "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Achxy/k-14-22", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "lean", "title": {"en": "Lean"}}, {"id": "4d", "title": {"en": "4D"}}, {"id": "abap", "title": {"en": "ABAP"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22722074"}}]}}, "title": "Failure of finite isolated generation for an irreducible centralizer over a polycyclic group", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722075", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722075", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722075?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722075", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722075", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722075", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722075/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722074", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722074", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722074", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zeno